            {
                "entry_id": "df09f810-2b20-3f53-add3-e7a05b40ff4e",
                "word": "hoove",
                "pos": "verb",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "7acc1135-d5c0-4d51-8f57-0e253e62153d",
                        "entry_id": "df09f810-2b20-3f53-add3-e7a05b40ff4e",
                        "tags": [
                            "present",
                            "singular",
                            "third-person"
                        ],
                        "form": "hooves"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "d1f7f680-ccbf-4fe8-a8d8-1884a79ca681",
                        "entry_id": "df09f810-2b20-3f53-add3-e7a05b40ff4e",
                        "tags": [
                            "participle",
                            "present"
                        ],
                        "form": "hooving"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "e8978855-8dba-4945-b8bb-243996df3208",
                        "entry_id": "df09f810-2b20-3f53-add3-e7a05b40ff4e",
                        "tags": [
                            "participle",
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "hooved"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "23ebc226-d6aa-418d-a09a-5bfe53650455",
                        "entry_id": "df09f810-2b20-3f53-add3-e7a05b40ff4e",
                        "tags": [
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "hooved"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ecc93d69-6b91-3aae-b181-405d5db66769",
                        "entry_id": "df09f810-2b20-3f53-add3-e7a05b40ff4e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Alternative form of hoof."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "alt-of",
                            "alternative"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8626d221-a14a-4683-87e8-5430157d6b54",
                                "sense_id": "ecc93d69-6b91-3aae-b181-405d5db66769",
                                "text": "In her father’s pasture was a bull and when it stamped and hooved the ground and bellowed below the trees it was a preacher and now the Preacher was a bull."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f79fc144-1358-49a7-bf04-ad9feaacf7e3",
                                "sense_id": "ecc93d69-6b91-3aae-b181-405d5db66769",
                                "text": "They had left soft ridges where they had hooved the ground up with their snoots and baby hands."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "961bba90-35f8-40b4-b190-8763badc6d57",
                                "sense_id": "ecc93d69-6b91-3aae-b181-405d5db66769",
                                "text": "[…] I didn’t find it, but came upon a cow moose blind, stinking with heat, moaning, and hooving the black peat with such blood, such fury, the woods broke open, the earth recovered her children, her silences, her poems."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1242ae73-d640-4b63-943f-9766129714ca",
                                "sense_id": "ecc93d69-6b91-3aae-b181-405d5db66769",
                                "text": "white heat red sunfired horses / tails swishing snakes / galloping / we were riders lion / headed hooving the hard ground / dust and cloud dragon and angel"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1ffdd64e-5d94-483a-bbe0-733abccdf42e",
                                "sense_id": "ecc93d69-6b91-3aae-b181-405d5db66769",
                                "text": "Cows, or something bigger, hoove the ground, pick at it, shovel up the dirt around my foot."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "398dd294-2b12-4b89-83a0-2346607fe631",
                                "sense_id": "ecc93d69-6b91-3aae-b181-405d5db66769",
                                "text": "A spoonbill stalks its future with primaeval staggers: so, this is Grace? he wonders cutting twine from pulpy bails, the sheep congregating and snorting air that is sharp, shaking glimmers of an indolent sun from burr-bitten wool, hooving the ground."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f49685d2-862c-4547-b652-d1331c125f06",
                                "sense_id": "ecc93d69-6b91-3aae-b181-405d5db66769",
                                "text": "What I want is Montana at Gold Rush: fevered, muscled horses hooving the elevations rushing fortunes in ice streams, hearts pumped white to bursting, passion pressed as sweat and hair into the back, the ache ridden to powder, steel shattered, and rock."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "015b680c-4df0-4a65-9c4a-4694380fd981",
                                "sense_id": "ecc93d69-6b91-3aae-b181-405d5db66769",
                                "text": "The animals, wild-drunk on country wine, hooved the ground, lacking a quarry, which was soon provided for them—another pig, followed by a wild chase to kill it."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f0cc00d3-fe5b-4770-a274-244323635bde",
                                "sense_id": "ecc93d69-6b91-3aae-b181-405d5db66769",
                                "text": "Each day I awake to hear them in my suburban hell, hooving the barn door, escaping through scented pastures with carefree defiance of the runaway!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "50677ab3-0ad3-42f7-a593-2744f8e6c585",
                                "sense_id": "ecc93d69-6b91-3aae-b181-405d5db66769",
                                "text": "When I bugle a second time, appending some vulgar grunts to the end, all hell cuts loose, the bull screaming back his rage, hooving the ground and horning trees to create a cacophony of hollow knocks that echo eerily through the forest gloom."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2e336859-12cb-4aa0-b50b-4b1642e0587c",
                                "sense_id": "ecc93d69-6b91-3aae-b181-405d5db66769",
                                "text": "They, model loyal workers, were doing their daily tasks; Steve, helped by Rodríguez, was cooking and preparing breakfast and Miss Carrol was hooving the red elegant carpet that is around the house, from the main entrance to the attic, passing by the rooms on the second floor."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d92f7ec5-acea-43f9-a9a4-2d0a7d435542",
                                "sense_id": "ecc93d69-6b91-3aae-b181-405d5db66769",
                                "text": "Across the yard, goats hooved the ground and rubbed their horns on the cedar posts of their fenced pen."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e88411b1-53df-4f2b-9fb1-5f42ebcb0b63",
                                "sense_id": "ecc93d69-6b91-3aae-b181-405d5db66769",
                                "text": "The sign records that a young boy was killed by a deer at this particular spot with a rather graphic picture of the said beast hooving the poor kid on the head."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c7a74c7d-c490-420a-a612-15f00f29d669",
                                "sense_id": "ecc93d69-6b91-3aae-b181-405d5db66769",
                                "text": "She ordered herself to declare, at least, what it was that frightened her on the other side of the flap. Was there a congress of rattlesnakes at the foot of her tent? A boar hooving the dust in anticipation of sinking a tusk into her flank?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "483e2b9e-9e38-4d3e-a0b4-4b57e0bb7ff2",
                                "sense_id": "ecc93d69-6b91-3aae-b181-405d5db66769",
                                "text": "He hooves the ground furiously. Kettlebell looks up at his rider. A winnie, and more hooving the ground."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "058c581d-8dd3-4a88-87f1-1ddb028c6511",
                                "sense_id": "ecc93d69-6b91-3aae-b181-405d5db66769",
                                "text": "Beneath him, his steed hooved the ground and snorted impatiently."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f29e7e06-1da2-4bbd-8be3-3698d69a3c76",
                                "sense_id": "ecc93d69-6b91-3aae-b181-405d5db66769",
                                "text": "Heart in her throat, she stood frozen in place as the gelding hooved the ground, but finally it seemed to settle."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c731834a-a9a8-4b52-951f-1fa7dcdfec3e",
                                "sense_id": "ecc93d69-6b91-3aae-b181-405d5db66769",
                                "text": "Bella stood and hooved the ground, moving hay around."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
